Menu-loop reloc-applier sites: route the DGROUP:0x12 (far install f842) and DGROUP:0x16 (near/far-form
clear f860->f869) service calls to the faithful shim appliers -- fixes the FLAKY (nondeterministic) SIGSEGV
that patches 125/126 exposed on the static main menu.

ROOT CAUSE (watchpoint + segv-EIP proven).  Patches 125/126 advanced execution into the main MENU LOOP
(FUN_0000_00d0: `while (FUN_1000_5c5f(), !stop) { FUN_1000_5c3a(); FUN_0000_cae6(); }`).  Every iteration
FUN_1000_5c3a installs a method-vector reloc section via `xor bx,bx; mov si,0xNNN; lcall [DGROUP:0x12]`
(the FAR applier FUN_0000_f842) and FUN_1000_5c5f tears the same vectors down via `lcall [DGROUP:0x16]`
(the clear applier FUN_0000_f860->f869); FUN_1000_2ebe (boot setup) installs si=0x1b8 the same way.
Ghidra dropped BOTH the BX/SI section operands at the indirect call site AND the x86 string-op segment
bases inside f842/f860/f869, so the engine's own appliers are inert and the raw `(*[c012])()`/`(*[c016])()`
far-calls ran the base-lost C bodies on UNINITIALISED register-arg garbage.  f842: `if (param_1 != 0) {
uVar1 = *param_3; ... }` -- param_1 (the dropped BX, asm `or bx,bx; je` guards it =0) is a garbage local:
when it happens to be nonzero the body dereferences the garbage param_3 host pointer -> SIGSEGV.  The
garbage varies run-to-run (stale stack), so the crash is FLAKY (~30-40%), and since the appliers run every
menu frame the whole static menu is nondeterministic.  segv EIP = 0x0808c0e4/0x0808c113 = FUN_0000_f842
fist.c:36484/36490; callers FUN_1000_2ebe:44128 and FUN_1000_5c3a:53656/58/59; fault-addr ~0xffff (garbage
param_3).  This is the doctrine-established DGROUP:0x12/0x16 reloc-service class (patches 022/030/031/053):
the loader-role shim applies the section faithfully from the game's OWN reloc table (seg 0x3352, base-0
identity) -- nothing invented.

FIX (asm-verified vs 0x12ebe/0x15c3a/0x15c5f):
- 2ebe: `xor bx,bx; mov si,0x1b8; lcall [0x12]` -> fist_apply_reloc_section(0x1b8,1) (installs the event
  handler vectors DGROUP:0x426..0x442 = 0xf69:0x3943.. ).
- 5c3a: three far installs -> fist_apply_reloc_section(0x3b0/0x3bc/0x3c8,1) (installs DGROUP:0x1692..0x16a6,
  incl. 0x1696/0x169e that 5c5f then calls); the 0x3b0 one keeps its `[0x2cc0]==0x8a57` gate.
- 5c5f: two installed-handler calls [0x1696]/[0x169e] kept verbatim, then three clears -> the new shim
  fist_zero_reloc_section(0x3c8/0x3bc/0x3b0) (asm order 15c6c/15c75/15c7e), the faithful f860->f869
  vector tear-down (DGROUP[off]=0, DGROUP[off+2]=0, leading seg word skipped).
